1
00:00:18,210 --> 00:00:19,250
That...

2
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:28,380
must have been a spirit.

3
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:29,960
Gadiel.

4
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,040
Your Majesty.

5
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:40,170
Rovel Vankreift will soon arrive
at the castle with his daughter.

6
00:00:41,210 --> 00:00:43,040
I intend to introduce you.

7
00:00:44,630 --> 00:00:45,670
Yes, sire.

8
00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:19,250
THE SIGNIFICANCE OF THE SPIRIT FESTIVAL

9
00:02:19,330 --> 00:02:23,670
My goodness! Ellen, dear, you look so cute!

10
00:02:23,750 --> 00:02:25,080
Far beyond my imagination!

11
00:02:25,830 --> 00:02:26,830
You too, Rovel.

12
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:29,540
Please don't add that like an afterthought.

13
00:02:31,580 --> 00:02:33,580
The carriage is ready, my lord.

14
00:02:33,670 --> 00:02:35,130
My apologies, Roren.

15
00:02:35,540 --> 00:02:38,250
I think we'll use my
teleportation spell this time.

16
00:02:38,330 --> 00:02:40,670
I see. Very well, my lord.

17
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:44,960
Father, you're thinking
how terrible it would be

18
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:48,500
for a driver if we needed to escape, aren't you?

19
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:50,130
You're a sharp one, Ellen.

20
00:02:50,670 --> 00:02:52,420
Do your best, Ellen, my dear!

21
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:54,670
Don't you lose to that blackhearted man!

22
00:02:54,750 --> 00:02:55,880
Godspeed, Brother.

23
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:58,960
It's not like we're going
there to fight, you know.

24
00:03:01,420 --> 00:03:04,880
Darling, be sure to protect Ellen, okay?

25
00:03:05,630 --> 00:03:06,960
Well then, we're off!

26
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:09,540
Go get 'em, Ellen!

27
00:03:09,630 --> 00:03:10,670
Excuse us.

28
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:25,630
Ah, I don't wanna, I don't wanna,
I don't wanna, I don't wanna...

29
00:03:25,710 --> 00:03:28,460
Father, there's no point lamenting it.

30
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:30,580
Let's go settle this once and for all!

31
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:34,210
Ellen, why does it seem like
you're all pumped up for this?

32
00:03:34,290 --> 00:03:38,830
To tell you the truth, I want to speak
with Mr. Blackheart directly.

33
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:42,790
Now let us proceed, Father!

34
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:45,960
Why do I only get a bad feeling about this?

35
00:03:49,250 --> 00:03:50,290
It's Lord Rovel!

36
00:03:50,380 --> 00:03:51,670
Open the gates!

37
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:55,790
Who is the girl with Lord Rovel?

38
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:57,130
Who knows?

39
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:02,040
Lord Rovel has arrived.

40
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:11,000
I've been waiting for you, Rovel.

41
00:04:11,380 --> 00:04:13,960
And you, little princess.

42
00:04:24,330 --> 00:04:25,830
Nice to meet you, Your Majesty.

43
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:28,330
I am Rovel's daughter, Ellen.

44
00:04:28,920 --> 00:04:32,040
How I've looked forward to meeting you, Ellen.

45
00:04:32,830 --> 00:04:34,000
Is that so?

46
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:39,790
There we have it.
You truly are Rovel's daughter.

47
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:43,040
Forgive me, Your Majesty,
but I do <i>not</i> want to hear that.

48
00:04:43,130 --> 00:04:45,170
Meanie! How could you, Ellen?!

49
00:04:45,250 --> 00:04:49,130
Ellen, what's going on lately?!
Isn't this a bit much for a rebellious phase?!

50
00:04:49,210 --> 00:04:52,210
- You're going to make your father cry!
- Father, your true colors are showing.

51
00:04:55,670 --> 00:04:57,420
Well, please have a seat.

52
00:05:00,460 --> 00:05:03,080
So you're that jovial beneath it all, eh?

53
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:07,170
Ever since I was little,
I was forced to discipline myself.

54
00:05:07,630 --> 00:05:10,580
I apologize for your engagement to Agiel.

55
00:05:11,170 --> 00:05:13,790
However, it was my father's decision.

56
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:17,170
They are no longer here.

57
00:05:17,250 --> 00:05:18,290
They aren't?

58
00:05:20,210 --> 00:05:25,630
Agiel, who has caused the problem,
and my father, who took responsibility,

59
00:05:25,710 --> 00:05:28,080
have moved to a castle in the hinterlands.

60
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:31,250
They will never return here again.

61
00:05:33,670 --> 00:05:38,460
<i>He used his little sister's misdeeds</i>
<i>to dethrone his father.</i>

62
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:41,830
<i>This man really is blackhearted.</i>

63
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:44,920
Still, how unfortunate for Sauvel.

64
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:48,630
To think his new wife turned out
to be just like Agiel.

65
00:05:48,710 --> 00:05:49,830
What do you mean?

66
00:05:50,420 --> 00:05:52,710
There's no way you haven't noticed.

67
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:55,960
It's the current gossip among the nobility.

68
00:05:56,580 --> 00:05:57,750
Father...

69
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:01,500
Why is such gossip going around?

70
00:06:02,170 --> 00:06:04,920
It's nothing a little princess
like yourself needs to hear.

71
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,460
That is a lie.

72
00:06:08,170 --> 00:06:13,000
You brought it up, fully aware that I was
capable of comprehending the conversation.

73
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:17,750
Ah, now I see how you managed to sway Alberto.

74
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:21,670
Your Majesty, you are a nasty man.

75
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:26,580
Uncle Alberto came pleading to you
about the Vankreift family's dilemma,

76
00:06:26,670 --> 00:06:29,880
and you took advantage of him.

77
00:06:31,750 --> 00:06:36,290
If I'm honest, I would've had
no issue using him as a double agent,

78
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:37,710
but I decided against it.

79
00:06:37,790 --> 00:06:39,330
Oh?

80
00:06:39,420 --> 00:06:43,250
I don't know what you think
of Uncle Alberto, Your Majesty,

81
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:47,580
but I don't believe he's cut out to be a spy.

82
00:06:49,630 --> 00:06:51,130
This is better than I had expected!

83
00:06:51,210 --> 00:06:53,460
Rovel, you're amazing!

84
00:06:53,540 --> 00:06:55,630
Just look at the girl you raised!

85
00:06:57,210 --> 00:07:03,420
Now then, you already know, don't you?
The origin of the rumors about Sauvel's wife...

86
00:07:03,790 --> 00:07:05,250
Are you testing me?

87
00:07:07,460 --> 00:07:11,330
You're attempting to leverage this rumor
to negotiate with my father.

88
00:07:11,420 --> 00:07:15,170
However, the rumor has already spread.

89
00:07:16,580 --> 00:07:19,540
Which means you weren't
the one to put it out there.

90
00:07:20,170 --> 00:07:21,750
Who was it, then?

91
00:07:22,750 --> 00:07:24,000
It was the queen.

92
00:07:24,580 --> 00:07:26,210
What makes you say that?

93
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:31,630
The way Aunt Aria looked at my father...
I think any woman would have noticed.

94
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:35,750
Then she would have realized
something was afoot when

95
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:38,290
the reception was canceled midway through.

96
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:39,960
And?

97
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:45,250
The thing is, it's not easy to spread rumors
about a ducal family like the Vankreifts.

98
00:07:45,330 --> 00:07:49,750
So the gossip must have come
from someone of equal or higher standing.

99
00:07:50,710 --> 00:07:54,580
Which leads me to suspect Queen Lalar.

100
00:07:56,380 --> 00:07:58,040
Incredible!

101
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:03,750
I haven't said a single word
about the condemnation.

102
00:08:03,830 --> 00:08:05,130
Condemnation?

103
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:07,580
What is he talking about?

104
00:08:07,670 --> 00:08:08,710
Who knows?

105
00:08:09,170 --> 00:08:13,380
Here I thought the rumor about Aunt Aria
concerned her bad habit with men.

106
00:08:13,460 --> 00:08:14,960
What condemnation do you mean?

107
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:17,040
I speak of Goddess Vár's condemnation.

108
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:21,630
Is there not a thorny bruise
on Sauvel's wife's wrist?

109
00:08:22,460 --> 00:08:24,460
Just as Agiel had.

110
00:08:25,250 --> 00:08:28,290
Know that hiding it will only
cause more trouble later.

111
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:33,080
I have never seen a thorny bruise.

112
00:08:33,170 --> 00:08:37,710
Father, I can see the royal family
doesn't care for us.

113
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:43,580
But even so, I never would have imagined
them stooping to baseless rumors.

114
00:08:43,670 --> 00:08:45,580
Truly, Ellen.

115
00:08:45,670 --> 00:08:48,330
It's unpleasant, so why don't we head home?

116
00:08:48,420 --> 00:08:49,790
Yes, Father!

117
00:08:51,790 --> 00:08:53,630
We're not done talking yet.

118
00:08:55,330 --> 00:08:58,540
It seems I've been given to speculation.

119
00:08:58,630 --> 00:09:00,790
Allow me to apologize for that.

120
00:09:01,670 --> 00:09:04,250
I'll inform my wife she was mistaken.

121
00:09:04,580 --> 00:09:06,500
Are you certain you want to do that?

122
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:07,920
Why do you ask?

123
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:12,790
What becomes of the royal family's reputation
if the rumor they spread is taken back?

124
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:17,420
I wasn't expecting you to be this good.

125
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:22,130
But are <i>you</i> certain
you want to leave things as they are?

126
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:24,920
This was your very intention
from the start, was it not?

127
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,250
Reason being, you already swore to my father

128
00:09:27,330 --> 00:09:32,580
that you'd bring me here
before the rumor ever spread.

129
00:09:33,330 --> 00:09:34,420
Hey, Ellen.

130
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:37,880
Won't you come be <i>my</i> daughter?

131
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:42,040
Your Majesty! You said you would limit
your contact with my family!

132
00:09:42,380 --> 00:09:44,000
Did I now?

133
00:09:44,630 --> 00:09:49,500
I refuse! My father is the only father I need.

134
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:50,960
Ellen!

135
00:09:51,580 --> 00:09:53,130
You're such a good girl!

136
00:09:53,210 --> 00:09:56,630
I can't believe this is the
true face of the hero.

137
00:09:58,170 --> 00:10:01,630
- You're such a good girl!
- Actually, I'd planned to introduce my sons—

138
00:10:01,710 --> 00:10:03,750
No, that won't be necessary.

139
00:10:03,830 --> 00:10:05,460
Bring in my sons.

140
00:10:05,540 --> 00:10:06,500
Sire!

141
00:10:06,580 --> 00:10:09,290
Ellen, I'm certain you'll like them as well.

142
00:10:10,250 --> 00:10:13,630
Both are very popular with the girls
from other families.

143
00:10:13,710 --> 00:10:16,750
Are you certain they're not
just after money and power?

144
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:19,830
I'm sure their parents are.

145
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:23,630
However, the girls do genuinely love my sons.

146
00:10:23,710 --> 00:10:25,670
They sound rather popular.

147
00:10:25,750 --> 00:10:28,420
So it seems you have no need of me.

148
00:10:28,750 --> 00:10:31,920
They're also quite good-looking,
if I say so myself.

149
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:36,250
I'm used to my parents,
so good looks mean nothing to me.

150
00:10:37,460 --> 00:10:39,420
Now then, let us go home, Father.

151
00:10:39,500 --> 00:10:40,920
You said it.

152
00:10:42,210 --> 00:10:45,460
Just what is your daughter made of, Rovel?

153
00:10:46,040 --> 00:10:49,170
There is no way you can win
against her, Your Majesty.

154
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:52,380
Even I can't, and I'm her father.

155
00:10:53,170 --> 00:10:54,290
I see.

156
00:10:55,420 --> 00:10:56,580
Come in.

157
00:10:57,580 --> 00:10:59,380
Pardon us, Father.

158
00:10:59,460 --> 00:11:00,500
Pardon us.

159
00:11:00,580 --> 00:11:02,420
Oh, you're here.

160
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:04,040
Let me introduce you.

161
00:11:04,630 --> 00:11:06,670
My eldest is Gadiel, age twelve.

162
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:09,500
My youngest is Rasel, age nine.

163
00:11:11,960 --> 00:11:14,710
This is Rovel the hero
and his daughter, Ellen.

164
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:23,750
I am Rovel Vankreift.

165
00:11:24,420 --> 00:11:25,960
It's an honor to meet you.

166
00:11:26,040 --> 00:11:28,710
A-Are you really the hero?!

167
00:11:28,790 --> 00:11:30,830
Now, Rasel, don't you think you're being rude?

168
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:32,750
Oh, I'm sorry.

169
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:45,420
Are you being shy?

170
00:11:45,790 --> 00:11:46,880
No.

171
00:11:49,830 --> 00:11:53,250
Are you okay? Are you not feeling well?

172
00:11:56,250 --> 00:11:57,830
Don't come near me!

173
00:12:07,250 --> 00:12:08,960
Are you really all right?

174
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:12,750
If she's unwell, why don't we let her rest?

175
00:12:16,250 --> 00:12:17,330
Stay back!

176
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:27,460
Spirits?

177
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:31,330
What in the world is going on?

178
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:34,250
This is why I didn't want
her to see them.

179
00:12:34,630 --> 00:12:35,880
What are you talking about?

180
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:41,420
<i>Help me! It hurts! Help me!</i>

181
00:12:43,630 --> 00:12:46,040
Is this... Are you asking me?

182
00:12:49,250 --> 00:12:52,130
<i>Help... me...</i>

183
00:12:52,210 --> 00:12:54,420
No!

184
00:13:02,170 --> 00:13:03,880
What on earth is that?!

185
00:13:10,460 --> 00:13:11,540
This is...

186
00:13:11,630 --> 00:13:13,500
Oh, spirit queen!

187
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:18,920
In order to turn the tide of the
Monster Tempest, lend us your power!

188
00:13:21,380 --> 00:13:24,080
Damn you! Why isn't it opening?

189
00:13:24,170 --> 00:13:29,250
In that case, use the spirit wizards
as bait to lure the spirits here!

190
00:13:29,330 --> 00:13:30,670
- Stop!
- Why?!

191
00:13:30,750 --> 00:13:33,210
- This isn't what we agreed on!
- After all we've done for this country...

192
00:13:33,290 --> 00:13:34,380
What are you doing?!

193
00:13:34,460 --> 00:13:35,750
We have to save them!

194
00:13:36,130 --> 00:13:39,960
Good! Now sacrifice the spirits!

195
00:13:44,790 --> 00:13:45,880
What?

196
00:13:46,420 --> 00:13:47,790
It hurts!

197
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:48,960
Can't breathe...

198
00:13:50,170 --> 00:13:52,210
Help me!

199
00:13:52,290 --> 00:13:53,540
Why?

200
00:13:54,460 --> 00:13:56,750
Stop! Stop!

201
00:13:56,830 --> 00:13:58,000
Ellen?

202
00:14:06,710 --> 00:14:10,710
Open the gate! Open the gate!

203
00:14:10,920 --> 00:14:16,250
Oh, spirit queen!
Hurry and lend us your power!

204
00:14:16,330 --> 00:14:17,920
<i>Why?!</i>

205
00:14:27,790 --> 00:14:29,920
<i>It hurts!</i>

206
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:34,580
<i>Help me... Help me!</i>

207
00:14:34,670 --> 00:14:37,290
N... No!

208
00:14:37,380 --> 00:14:40,830
Don't you dare touch my daughter!

209
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:46,630
<i>Help me! Please!</i>

210
00:14:53,710 --> 00:14:54,750
Rovel...

211
00:14:56,210 --> 00:14:59,580
If this continues, we'll lose our minds too.

212
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:02,540
Rovel, what in the world is...

213
00:15:02,630 --> 00:15:04,500
You still don't understand?

214
00:15:04,750 --> 00:15:08,000
This is the spirit curse placed
upon you and the royal family!

215
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,420
It's all right. It's all right.

216
00:15:13,670 --> 00:15:15,880
Come now, let's hurry home.

217
00:15:20,250 --> 00:15:23,880
A curse? So that's what this is...

218
00:15:32,250 --> 00:15:34,040
Ellen? Ellen!

219
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:35,580
Ellen, dear.

220
00:15:37,130 --> 00:15:38,170
Ori!

221
00:15:41,710 --> 00:15:44,330
You're okay. You're okay now.

222
00:15:44,420 --> 00:15:47,750
Sweet Ellen. Let's take a little nap, okay?

223
00:15:50,460 --> 00:15:53,080
Is Ellen all right? She's...

224
00:15:54,460 --> 00:15:57,630
She has a fever, but there's no need to worry.

225
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:04,960
As I thought, it was too soon.

226
00:16:05,210 --> 00:16:08,460
You're right. I shouldn't have let them meet.

227
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:13,630
It seemed like they saw the curse too.

228
00:16:14,170 --> 00:16:15,790
Ellen must be the cause.

229
00:16:16,790 --> 00:16:22,880
The spirits realized she was my daughter
and started to ask her for help.

230
00:16:25,080 --> 00:16:27,130
He seems stable, but...

231
00:16:27,210 --> 00:16:28,170
I see.

232
00:16:28,250 --> 00:16:29,500
How terrifying...

233
00:16:31,330 --> 00:16:33,920
Your Majesty! Are you all right?

234
00:16:34,790 --> 00:16:36,080
How are my sons?

235
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:38,290
Do not push yourself!

236
00:16:39,710 --> 00:16:43,130
They are both unconscious, but they are safe.

237
00:16:44,460 --> 00:16:45,670
I see.

238
00:17:18,540 --> 00:17:19,580
Brother?

239
00:17:20,750 --> 00:17:22,170
Let us go back as well.

240
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:23,790
Yeah.

241
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:29,500
I wonder if these prayers
truly reach the spirits.

242
00:17:30,460 --> 00:17:33,790
We offer them every year
at the Spirit Festival,

243
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:36,080
but it happened two hundred years ago.

244
00:17:36,170 --> 00:17:39,830
You'd think they would
have forgiven us by now.

245
00:17:40,540 --> 00:17:45,920
Besides, it had nothing to do
with us... Don't you think?

246
00:17:47,960 --> 00:17:51,920
<i>Indeed, why </i>do<i> the spirits</i>
<i>avoid the royal family?</i>

247
00:17:52,670 --> 00:17:58,710
<i>The answer to that was written</i>
<i>in an old book I found in a hidden room.</i>

248
00:17:59,630 --> 00:18:01,420
<i>The things the royal family did,</i>

249
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:05,380
<i>the way they treated the spirits, and...</i>

250
00:18:06,380 --> 00:18:10,420
<i>how humans angered something</i>
<i>they shouldn't have.</i>

251
00:18:11,630 --> 00:18:17,580
<i>What I saw then—what that</i>
<i>thing was—I now know.</i>

252
00:18:20,830 --> 00:18:23,880
<i>This is where the tragedy</i>
<i>of two hundred years ago took place.</i>

253
00:18:25,130 --> 00:18:29,380
<i>There's no longer a need</i>
<i>for human prayers or regret over it.</i>

254
00:18:30,250 --> 00:18:34,630
<i>All that remains is our conflict</i>
<i>with the spirits, their wounds,</i>

255
00:18:34,710 --> 00:18:38,210
<i>and their unheard cries.</i>

256
00:18:53,170 --> 00:18:56,630
It's time for the Spirit Festival
again this year.

257
00:18:57,130 --> 00:18:58,290
Hey, Ellen.

258
00:18:59,040 --> 00:19:01,080
How have you been since then?

259
00:19:03,670 --> 00:19:05,960
I want to see you, if only for a moment.

260
00:19:07,250 --> 00:19:11,750
I just want to apologize to you.

261
00:19:16,040 --> 00:19:23,420
I wonder if the day will come that you
and the spirits ever forgive me.

262
00:19:30,460 --> 00:19:31,830
I'll be back.

263
00:19:52,920 --> 00:19:54,500
Well...

264
00:19:54,880 --> 00:20:01,460
You see, the great spirits wanted
humans to understand what they'd done.

265
00:20:02,170 --> 00:20:06,630
And so they decided
to cast a spell on the king

266
00:20:06,710 --> 00:20:08,290
that he would hear the spirits' cries.

267
00:20:08,750 --> 00:20:12,750
The king continued to hear
those cries until his death.

268
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:17,670
But the spell was only cast
upon the king at the time.

269
00:20:18,130 --> 00:20:21,880
So it couldn't have been passed
down to his descendants.

270
00:20:21,960 --> 00:20:24,960
Huh? Then why did it...

271
00:20:25,420 --> 00:20:32,170
With no place to go, the souls of the spirits
have clung to royal blood and cursed it.

272
00:20:32,670 --> 00:20:35,540
Then <i>that's</i> what the black mist is.

273
00:20:35,630 --> 00:20:40,330
Yes. And that's why the royal family
remains cursed to this very day.

274
00:20:42,380 --> 00:20:45,380
I know you went to the Spirit Festival.

275
00:20:46,710 --> 00:20:52,420
It's in your nature to worry, to hurt,
and to try to break the curse, Ellen.

276
00:20:53,330 --> 00:20:56,170
That's why I've never told you the details.

277
00:20:58,250 --> 00:21:00,710
Mother, I...

278
00:21:01,460 --> 00:21:05,960
I want to save my fellow
spirits who remain tortured.

279
00:21:06,380 --> 00:21:14,420
I want to free them of the pain, humiliation,
suffering, and anger they've endured.

280
00:21:17,420 --> 00:21:23,290
Ellen, dear.... I knew my
kind daughter would say that.

281
00:21:26,290 --> 00:21:30,750
Do I have the power to liberate those souls?

282
00:21:32,880 --> 00:21:34,750
I think it will be difficult.

283
00:21:36,960 --> 00:21:42,290
Humans only offer token prayers every year
at the Spirit Festival, you understand.

284
00:21:43,170 --> 00:21:45,630
Not only are they ungrateful for us spirits,

285
00:21:45,710 --> 00:21:48,960
but they've never reflected on what they did.

286
00:21:50,460 --> 00:21:53,880
That is why they remain unforgiven.

287
00:21:55,040 --> 00:21:58,540
I'm not one to speak, having
taken Rovel as my husband,

288
00:21:58,630 --> 00:22:05,830
but please do not involve yourself further
with the cursed humans and wandering spirits.

289
00:22:06,790 --> 00:22:12,290
That is my advice to you as a spirit,
as a goddess, and as your mother.

290
00:22:17,790 --> 00:22:18,790
Yes, ma'am.

